    "updated_at": "2022-12-16T13:16:48Z",
    "body": "\"No DOM at all apart from the Document object\" is more or less what's required; if you want access to some specific part of the document to work on you can register a mutation observer or similar; it's not expected that people will directly try to do DOM manipulation in the top level script. But the hard requirement is that it runs before any script on the page (similar to Web Extensions content scripts).",
