    "created_at": "2026-03-19T09:28:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-20T08:03:48Z",
    "body": "[This Playwright test](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/23b41bbc614d0f7776e0fff6d9fd7654d3893428/tests/page/page-add-init-script.spec.ts#L116-L129) is failing because\r\n- the preload script sometimes runs twice in a browsing context and\r\n- `location.href` is sometimes empty when it runs\r\n\r\nI'm guessing these issues are caused by what @domenic and @zcorpan pointed out in their comments:\r\n- the additional preload script run seems to be happening when the browsing context navigates from `about:blank` to an `http://` URL\r\n- the preload script runs before the navigation is committed\r\n\r\nI think we should address at least the second issue: test authors may want to write preload scripts with different behaviors depending on the URL that the browsing context is navigating to. The first issue should only be observable if the preload script writes to the console (or if it creates performance issues).",
